# Spruce CSS

> Spruce CSS is a Sass-based, minimalistic CSS framework. It styles native elements with a few classes and gives you variables, mixins and functions for your own components. Version 3 adds design style presets (data-spruce-style), a built-in dark mode, design tokens and AI skills.

- npm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/sprucecss
- Source: https://github.com/conedevelopment/sprucecss
- AI skills: https://github.com/conedevelopment/sprucecss/tree/main/skills
- Spruce UI index (JSON): {{ site.url }}/library.json

## Spruce UI

Spruce UI is the component library built on Spruce CSS: components, blocks (full-width page sections) and complete pages. It isn't in the npm package; every item has a Markdown endpoint with its rendered HTML, its SCSS, its JavaScript and its dependencies in loading order. The links below point to these endpoints (the same URL without `.md` is the preview page).

